# Build
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg

# Siemens / TIA
*.ap20.~*
Logs/
IM/
UserFiles/
System/
AdditionalFiles/
TMP/
*.tia_backup

# Do not version the Openness DLLs (Siemens property, they live in the local installation)
Siemens.Engineering*.dll

# Working exports (versioned snapshots go in export/)
tmp/
scratch/

# Personal Claude Code settings (holds the private ntfy topic)
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Governance: the audit trail is a local record of this machine, never shared history.
**/.tia-mcp/audit.jsonl

# Copies of overwritten state: local safety net for this machine, not shared history. They can
# also hold whole exported programs, which do not belong in a diff.
**/.tia-mcp/backups/

# The policy is per project and per machine; policy.example.json is the one that ships.
**/.tia-mcp/policy.json

# The harness (phase 3) is Node and TypeScript. Dependencies and build output are not history.
harness/node_modules/
harness/dist/
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/dist/
dashboard/.vite/

# The Anthropic API key the generator uses. Never history, on any machine.
.env
harness/.env

# What the harness produces on this machine: retrieved projects, which are large and are copies of
# an asset already in the repository, and the measurement store. The numbers get reported, with
# their sample size, in docs/STATUS.md; the database itself is a machine's record.
**/.tia-mcp/harness/

# The knowledge corpus (stage 1): manuals from Siemens, Universal Robots, SICK and Festo are
# copyrighted and are not redistributed here. What is versioned is the recipe — URL, hash, version —
# so each machine builds its own index from documents its owner is entitled to have.
harness/corpus/*
!harness/corpus/recipe.json
